FINAL ANSWER:
**Bus factor of `lib/` is 2 by commit count.** Troy Goode alone made 50% of the 66 commits, and the second author brings it past the threshold. The statistic is thin, though, because the numbers behind it are skewed.

- **Spread:** 25 authors have touched `lib/`. After Troy Goode, the next authors have 4, 4, 3 and 2 commits. No silo is flagged, because no one passes 80%.
- **Contributors:** Most of the 25 are one-off contributors, so the real set of people who know the code is probably small.
- **Line ownership:** `lib/` has one file, `lib/index.js` (238 lines). `git blame` credits 89.9% of it to "Fiona Formatter", with 8.4% to Troy Goode. That figure is misleading. "Fiona Formatter" is almost certainly the identity on the latest commit, `62628c0 style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes`. Blame credits those lines to the reformatter instead of the people who wrote the logic. I haven't checked this, for example with `git blame --ignore-rev 62628c0`.
- **Orphaned file:** The tool marks `lib/index.js` as orphaned. Every author with a meaningful share of its lines has no commit since 2026-04-22. Troy Goode's last commit was 2026-04-10, which makes the 50% commit owner inactive too. This result is skewed by the same reformat commit.

If Troy Goode and one more person leave, nobody who wrote most of the commits is left. Whether anyone still understands the code is a different question. It is a single 238-line file, so it is cheap to relearn. The open risk is the history behind its design decisions.

I can rerun blame with the reformat commit ignored, to see who owns the logic.

